cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SciFraudScan
message: >-
  If you use this toolkit in work you publish, please cite it, and cite the
  original methods it implements as well. The methods are listed in
  references/METHODOLOGY.md; this software only implements them.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shi
    given-names: Jiwei
repository-code: "https://github.com/kiwi0719/SciFraudScan"
abstract: >-
  Statistical screening for research data anomalies: GRIM and GRIMMER
  feasibility of reported means and SDs, recomputation of reported p-values,
  duplication and derived columns, terminal-digit preference, Carlisle-style
  baseline balance against an empirical reference, p-curve and caliper tests.
  Produces screening signals for triage, not findings of misconduct.
keywords:
  - research integrity
  - scientific fraud
  - data forensics
  - GRIM
  - GRIMMER
  - p-curve
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-09-21"
